{
  "info": {
    "name": "Bet Room Service API",
    "description": "Drives a full duel in the order the widget does: alice opens a room from a bet she has already placed, bob holds a seat and confirms it with his own, then alice offers a rematch only bob can take.\n\nRun the requests top to bottom \u2014 each one saves what the next needs into the environment. A pre-request script on the collection mints fresh bet references per run, because one bet can belong to at most one room.\n\nAUTHENTICATION: with AUTH_JWT_SECRET unset the server takes the bearer token itself as the caller's identity, which is what makes aliceToken/bobToken/carolToken three different people here. Set the secret and these need to be real HS256 tokens whose `sub` claim identifies the caller.\n\nThe tests assert the three wire-format facts that break the widget silently: success bodies are not enveloped, error bodies use `message` rather than `error`, and every timestamp is epoch milliseconds.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:5000"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Ping (public)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/ping",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "ping"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Liveness. One of only two routes that need no credential."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Limits without a credential -> 401",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/limits",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rooms",
            "limits"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Every room route needs a bearer credential: the payload carries no user identifier, so an unauthenticated request cannot be attributed to anyone."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "// The widget reads body.message and falls back to the HTTP status text.",
              "pm.test('error body uses message, not error', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.message).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('error');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Get limits",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{aliceToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/limits",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rooms",
            "limits"
          ]
        },
        "description": "The caller's duel limits and how many they have played today."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('reports a per-duel max and today\\'s count', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.perDuelMax).to.be.a('number');",
              "  pm.expect(body.playedToday).to.be.a('number');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Create room (alice)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{aliceToken}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rooms"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Alice opens a duel from a bet she has ALREADY placed \u2014 betRef is required, because creation places the bet before the room exists. The server derives capacity from the strategy and the figures from the stake and the two prices.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"eventId\": \"{{eventId}}\",\n  \"strategy\": \"duel\",\n  \"participant\": {\n    \"label\": \"Maksym K.\",\n    \"initials\": \"MK\",\n    \"balances\": {\n      \"eur\": 75.5\n    }\n  },\n  \"betRef\": {\n    \"id\": \"{{creatorBetId}}\",\n    \"number\": 12345\n  },\n  \"expiresAt\": {{expiresAt}},\n  \"payload\": {\n    \"marketId\": \"total_goals\",\n    \"marketItemId\": \"total_goals_2.5\",\n    \"creatorSide\": {\n      \"outcomeId\": \"over\",\n      \"odd\": 182,\n      \"placement\": {\n        \"stake\": 10.0,\n        \"lineItemId\": \"li-12\",\n        \"dataVersion\": 7\n      }\n    },\n    \"opponentSide\": {\n      \"outcomeId\": \"under\",\n      \"odd\": 205\n    },\n    \"figures\": {\n      \"payout\": 0,\n      \"entry\": 0,\n      \"pot\": 0\n    }\n  }\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "// Collection-scoped values, minted once here rather than on the collection:",
              "// a collection-level pre-request script runs before EVERY request, which",
              "// would change eventId between the create and the list that looks for it.",
              "// One bet can belong to at most one room, so every run needs fresh",
              "// references or the second pass hits the idempotency index.",
              "const stamp = Date.now();",
              "pm.environment.set('creatorBetId', 'bet-postman-' + stamp + '-a');",
              "pm.environment.set('joinerBetId', 'bet-postman-' + stamp + '-b');",
              "pm.environment.set('rematchBetId', 'bet-postman-' + stamp + '-c');",
              "pm.environment.set('eventId', 'evt-postman-' + stamp);",
              "// expiresAt is epoch MILLISECONDS, never RFC3339.",
              "pm.environment.set('expiresAt', stamp + 30 * 60 * 1000);"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
              "const room = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('body is the room itself, not an envelope', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(room).to.not.have.property('data');",
              "  pm.expect(room.id).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});",
              "pm.test('timestamps are epoch milliseconds', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(room.createdAt).to.be.a('number').and.be.above(1e12);",
              "  pm.expect(room.expiresAt).to.be.a('number').and.be.above(1e12);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('figures are derived: 10.00 at 1.82 vs 2.05', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(room.payload.figures.payout).to.eql(18.2);",
              "  pm.expect(room.payload.figures.entry).to.eql(8.87);",
              "  pm.expect(room.payload.figures.pot).to.eql(18.87);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('the reader is told which participant they are', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(room.viewerParticipantId).to.eql(room.participants[0].id);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('an invite code and a HOST-side link were issued', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(room.inviteCode).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "  pm.expect(room.inviteUrl).to.include('betRoomId=' + room.id);",
              "  pm.expect(room.inviteUrl).to.include('betRoomInvite=' + room.inviteCode);",
              "});",
              "pm.environment.set('roomId', room.id);",
              "pm.environment.set('inviteCode', room.inviteCode);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Read room (stranger, no code) -> 200 without the secret",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{carolToken}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/read",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rooms",
            "{{roomId}}",
            "read"
          ]
        },
        "description": "A caller who is neither a participant nor a code holder still reads the room: rooms are observable. What they do NOT get is inviteCode or inviteUrl -- the url embeds the code as betRoomInvite, so the two are withheld together, and a scraped room id never becomes a way to take the seat.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('room state is readable', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('status');",
              "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('participants');",
              "});",
              "pm.test('the invite secret is withheld', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.inviteCode, 'inviteCode').to.be.undefined;",
              "  pm.expect(body.inviteUrl, 'inviteUrl').to.be.undefined;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Read room (code holder)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{bobToken}}"
          },
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/read",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rooms",
            "{{roomId}}",
            "read"
          ]
        },
        "description": "POST, not GET: the invite code is a join secret and a query string is the one place it must never appear. A code holder who has not taken a seat gets no viewerParticipantId \u2014 there is no participant of theirs to name.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"inviteCode\": \"{{inviteCode}}\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const room = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('a code holder is not yet a participant', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(room.viewerParticipantId).to.be.undefined;",
              "  pm.expect(room.participants).to.have.lengthOf(1);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "4. List open rooms on the event (bob)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Authorization",
            "value": "Bearer {{bobToken}}"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms?eventId={{eventId}}&status=open",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "rooms"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "eventId",
              "value": "{{eventId}}"
            },
            {
              "key": "status",
              "value": "open"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Open rooms on an event, excluding the caller's own and every rematch. The invite code IS returned here: listing a duel on an event is the offer to anyone viewing it, so without the code nothing on the list could be taken."
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const rooms = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('alice\\'s duel is listed, with its code', () => {",
              "  const found = rooms.find(r => r.id === pm.environment.get('roomId'));",
              "  pm.expect(found, 'the duel was not listed').to.not.be.undefined;",
              "  pm.expect(found.inviteCode).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "5. List open rooms (alice) \u2014 her own are excluded",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
